==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|imperfeccion|lang=fro}}. See {{prefix|im|perfection|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɪmpɚˈfɛkʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛkʃən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} Those [[qualities]] or [[features]] that are imperfect; the characteristic, state, or quality of being [[imperfect]].
#: ''You can accept your '''imperfection''' or try to improve.''
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} Something that makes something else less than perfect; a [[blemish]], [[impurity]], [[error]], etc.
#: ''He loves me despite my '''imperfections'''.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|quality of being imperfect}} [[corruption]]
* {{sense|something that prevents perfection}} [[fault]], [[flaw]], [[mark]], [[problem]], [[weakness]]
* See also [[Wikisaurus:defect]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|quality of being imperfect}} [[flawlessness]], [[perfection]]

